From ef49da8be18b228a45b5a25210905575470d50d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Roessner <c@roessner.co>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 12:39:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] milter: pass event context to macro lookup

The macro lookup callback receives only a macro name and caller context.
This is insufficient when a value must be available for one Milter event
but not another. In particular, end-of-header and end-of-message macro
values are both resolved by milter_message().

Add an event-aware callback alternative and pass an internal event value at
each lookup site. Preserve milter_macro_callback() and its behavior for all
existing callers. This does not change the Milter wire protocol.

Add a regression test for every lookup event, including distinct EOH and
EOM values, and for switching back to the legacy callback.

Tested with:

    make -C src/milter tests
    make -j4
